    "written_findings": [
      "Forward central twist: projection into old middle plus unchanged untwisted end gives exact intersection; inductive end C-properties verified, converse not used.",
      "First-three-marks obstruction: if ac commutes with b then (ab)^2=(cb)^2 lies in <b>, but can equal neither1 nor b. Noncentral involutions in a nonabelian dihedral group are reflections; distinct commuting ones have central product. This replaces the old Suzuki classification citation with an elementary proof.",
      "Rank4 base: new two-end intersection lies in <a,c>=C2^2; any enlargement beyond<ac> makes <a,b,c> dihedral, impossible. The higher-rank induction explicitly checks both end C-properties, recovery/generation and exact middle intersection.",
      "Irreducibility: new first pair is covered by the triple lemma; new second pair cannot commute unless old r2,r3 commute. All other adjacent pairs unchanged.",
      "Recovery iff finite odd order: old submarking is independent C2 times the two-involution dihedral group. Odd order gives the displayed power identity; even/infinite order yields the character graph excluding the independent C2 generator. This is not necessity for every successful rank contraction.",
      "Iteration: next tested bond is original p4 and then p5, with a precise n-3 stopping bound. Symmetric path components give the original full IP directly.",
      "Alternating consequences retain exact highest-rank seeds: type[10,3^(R-2)] for m=1mod4,m>=13 and type[5,6,3^(R-6),6,6,3] for even m>=14. Only existence intervals3..R and6..R are deduced; classifications and other congruence cases are not imported as new consequences.",
      "Characteristic2 intervals retain complete BFL highest-rank generation/IP/Witt-type input with every adjacent order q+1. Odd-characteristic interval retains Monson-Schulte construction and group identification through the source statement. Gram recurrence is proved algebraically, with initial determinants3,-2,-16 and D(j+3)=-8D(j), so primes>=5 are nondegenerate.",
      "All four source matrices and all three source diagrams matched. Independent Python exact sets verify all172 matrix parabolic intersections, isometry/form count21, group order1440, both types and failed recovery. Separate permutation arithmetic verifies all six graph cancellations and exact type/orbit sizes. Fresh author GAP verifies all6240 A11 parabolic pairs and generation.",
      "The common theorem is attributed to Brooksbank-Leemans; the forward twist to Fernandes-Leemans-Mixer, classical construction seeds to their original authors. This packet does not establish historical novelty."
    ],
